{"id":"0849af5e5df35e4bb602d28f84429c243989687f","axis":"silent","repo":"apache/druid","sha":"0849af5e5df35e4bb602d28f84429c243989687f","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/development/extensions-core/s3.md","lines":["@@ -81,6 +81,24 @@ For more information, refer to the [Amazon Developer Guide](https://docs.aws.ama"," "," Alternatively, you can bypass this chain by specifying an access key and secret key using a [Properties Object](../../ingestion/input-sources.md#s3-input-source) inside your ingestion specification."," ","+Whichever credentials are resolved are then used to assume any `assumeRoleArn` named by an ingestion spec or export destination. Setting `druid.s3.intermediateAssumeRoleArn` inserts one role in between: the resolved credentials assume that role first, and the resulting credentials assume `assumeRoleArn`. Keys given in an ingestion spec's Properties Object skip the intermediate role and assume `assumeRoleArn` directly.","+","+Set `druid.s3.intermediateAssumeRoleArn` on every process that builds an S3 input source or export destination:","+","+* Peons, which run ingestion and export tasks. Peons inherit the Middle Manager's runtime properties, so set it in the Middle Manager's `runtime.properties`, or set `druid.indexer.fork.property.druid.s3.intermediateAssumeRoleArn` there to apply it to Peons only.","+* Indexers, which run tasks in their own process.","+* The Overlord, which runs the sampler used by the web console's data loader.","+","+A process that doesn't have the property set keeps assuming `assumeRoleArn` directly, so leaving it out of one of these causes the same ingestion to succeed on some processes and fail on others.","+","+:::warning","+","+Scope an intermediate role to a single trust boundary. Druid assumes it with no external ID, so every role that trusts it is reachable by every ingestion spec and `EXPORT` statement that any process using the role can run. If several clusters share one ARN, the bucket owner's trust policy can no longer tell those clusters apart, and a user of any one of them can assume any role that trusts the shared intermediate role.","+","+Note that `assumeRoleArn` and `assumeRoleExternalId` both come from whoever writes the spec or `EXPORT` statement, so the external ID doesn't restrict which roles a spec author can reach. Treat it as a value spec authors supply rather than a secret the cluster holds, and have the bucket owner's trust policy turn on something spec authors don't control, such as an intermediate role used by only one cluster.","+","+:::","+"," Use the property [`druid.startup.logging.maskProperties`](../../configuration/index.md#startup-logging) to mask credentials information in Druid logs. For example, `[\"password\", \"secretKey\", \"awsSecretAccessKey\"]`."," "," ### S3 permissions settings","@@ -127,6 +145,7 @@ For example, to set the region to 'us-east-1' through system properties:"," |`druid.s3.accessKey`|S3 access key. See [S3 authentication methods](#s3-authentication-methods) for more details|Can be omitted according to authentication methods chosen.|"," |`druid.s3.secretKey`|S3 secret key. See [S3 authentication methods](#s3-authentication-methods) for more details|Can be omitted according to authentication methods chosen.|"," |`druid.s3.fileSessionCredentials`|Path to properties file containing `sessionToken`, `accessKey` and `secretKey` value. One key/value pair per line (format `key=value`). See [S3 authentication methods](#s3-authentication-methods) for more details |Can be omitted according to authentication methods chosen.|","+|`druid.s3.intermediateAssumeRoleArn`|AWS ARN of a role to assume before assuming the `assumeRoleArn` given by an ingestion spec or export destination. Lets a bucket owner's trust policy name one fixed ARN instead of a different principal for every Druid cluster. See [S3 authentication methods](#s3-authentication-methods) for more details.|None|"," |`druid.s3.protocol`|Communication protocol type to use when sending requests to AWS. `http` or `https` can be used. This configuration would be ignored if `druid.s3.endpoint.url` is filled with a URL with a different protocol.|`https`|"," |`druid.s3.disableChunkedEncoding`|Disables chunked encoding. See [AWS document](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSJavaSDK/latest/javadoc/com/amazonaws/services/s3/AmazonS3Builder.html#disableChunkedEncoding--) for details.|false|"," |`druid.s3.enablePathStyleAccess`|Enables path style access. See [AWS document](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSJavaSDK/latest/javadoc/com/amazonaws/services/s3/AmazonS3Builder.html#enablePathStyleAccess--) for details.|false|"],"additions":19,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/ingestion/input-sources.md","lines":["@@ -212,7 +212,7 @@ Properties Object:"," "," :::info"," ","-If `accessKeyId` and `secretAccessKey` are not given, the default [S3 credentials provider chain](../development/extensions-core/s3.md#s3-authentication-methods) is used.","+If `accessKeyId` and `secretAccessKey` are not given, the default [S3 credentials provider chain](../development/extensions-core/s3.md#s3-authentication-methods) is used. If the Druid process sets `druid.s3.intermediateAssumeRoleArn`, the resolved credentials assume that role before assuming `assumeRoleArn`."," "," :::"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/multi-stage-query/reference.md","lines":["@@ -152,7 +152,7 @@ Supported arguments for the function:"," |---|---|---|---|"," | `bucket` | Yes  | S3 bucket destination for exported files. You must add the bucket and prefix combination to the `druid.export.storage.s3.allowedExportPaths` allow list. | n/a |"," | `prefix` | Yes  | Destination path in the bucket to create exported files. The export query expects the destination path to be empty. If the location includes other files, the query will fail. You must add the bucket and prefix combination to the `druid.export.storage.s3.allowedExportPaths` allow list. | n/a |","-| `assumeRoleArn` | No | ARN of the role to assume before exporting data. If not provided, the default credentials configured for the Druid process are used. | n/a |","+| `assumeRoleArn` | No | ARN of the role to assume before exporting data. If not provided, the default credentials configured for the Druid process are used. If provided and the Druid process sets `druid.s3.intermediateAssumeRoleArn`, those credentials assume that role before assuming `assumeRoleArn`. | n/a |"," | `assumeRoleExternalId` | No | External ID to use when assuming the role specified in assumeRoleArn. This provides an additional layer of security for role assumption. Only used when assumeRoleArn is set. | n/a |"," "," Configure the following runtime parameters to export to an S3 destination:"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions-core/s3-extensions/pom.xml","lines":["@@ -142,6 +142,11 @@","       <artifactId>auth</artifactId>","       <version>${aws.sdk.v2.version}</version>","     </dependency>","+    <dependency>","+      <groupId>software.amazon.awssdk</groupId>","+      <artifactId>identity-spi</artifactId>","+      <version>${aws.sdk.v2.version}</version>","+    </dependency>","     <dependency>","       <groupId>software.amazon.awssdk</groupId>","       <artifactId>sdk-core</artifactId>"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions-core/s3-extensions/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/data/input/s3/S3InputSource.java","lines":["@@ -129,7 +129,9 @@ public S3InputSource(","           awsEndpointConfig,","           awsClientConfig,","           s3InputSourceConfig,","-          null","+          null,","+          s3ClientBuilder.getIntermediateRoleConfig(),","+          s3ClientBuilder.getIntermediateRoleEndpointConfig()","       ).build();","     });","     this.maxRetries = RetryUtils.DEFAULT_MAX_TRIES;"],"additions":3,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions-core/s3-extensions/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/storage/s3/S3IntermediateRoleConfig.jav